Subject: [PATCH 06941/11362] [outer-loop] ARC perception-grounding audit
 (Sensi failure-mode check)

Addresses task 1 of ops/known-issues.md's 2026-07-06 ARC standing-floor
queue (perception-grounding audit, cheap, run first). Diagnostic only, no
code changes, per the task's own scope ("report findings before proposing a
fix").

Audited arc_frame_change_predictor.py and arc_online_action_effect_scorer.py
against the failure mode arXiv:2603.17683 ("Sensi") describes: an LLM-as-
judge validating its own hallucinated frame-diff reads as internally
self-consistent rather than against ground truth.

Finding 1 (positive): the live frame-diff scorer
(GroundTruthValidatedFrameChangeScorer) gates its ranking influence behind
agreement with real observed pixel deltas, disabling itself permanently on
any single contradiction -- it is a numeric CNN+memory scorer, not an LLM
doing free-text self-assessment, so it cannot exhibit the literal Sensi
pattern. Tier-3 induced world-model code is similarly checked by running it
against held-out real transitions (WorldModelVerifier), not by trusting the
proposer's own confidence -- this session's own exp5588/exp5589 runs
demonstrate that gate correctly rejecting low-accuracy induced engines
rather than trusting them.

Finding 2 (real, unrelated to Sensi, live-path-active): traced a
project-documented but never-fixed-on-the-shipped-path bug --
FrameChangeScorer.candidate_score's getattr(candidate, "action_id") raises
AttributeError on dict-shaped candidates, silently zeroing the CNN term.
arc_online_action_effect_scorer.py's own docstring already documents this
as a measured ~20/25-games false-negative cause, but its fix
(_as_action_like) was only ever applied in that research-only scorer
variant, never backported to the shipped arc_frame_change_predictor.py
classes. Confirmed this fires on the live DEFAULT path (not just an
optional/disabled feature) via ActionEffectExpansionPrior.frontier_priority,
gated only by SUBMITTED_ACTION_EFFECT_EXPANSION_PRIOR_ENABLED=True -- every
frontier-priority computation on the shipped agent silently drops the CNN's
already-small (cnn_weight=0.05) contribution. Honestly bounded: given the
small weight and the project's own prior LOO=chance finding on frame-only
features, this audit does not establish how much capability the bug costs,
only that it is real and confirmed live.

Both findings corroborate rather than contradict
project_arc_live_agent_learning_gaps' standing conclusion that the binding
constraint is perception REPRESENTATION quality, not validation discipline
-- the grounding machinery here is unusually careful.

Full write-up: docs/research-notes/arc-perception-grounding-audit-2026-07-13.md.
